<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Beyşehir</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Beyşehir Gölü</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beysehir">Beyşehir</a> is a large freshwater lake in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, in the provinces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konya">Konya</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isparta">Isparta</a>, and the largest freshwater lake in the country. The Seljuk sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kayqubad-i">Kayqubad I</a> built the palace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kubadabad-palace">Kubadabad</a> on its shore in the 1230s, and the town of Beyşehir at its south-eastern end became the capital of the Eşrefoğlu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-beysehir.jpg" alt="Lake Beyşehir" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Earth Science and Remote Sensing Unit, NASA Johnson Space Center · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ISS061-E-14351_-_View_of_Earth.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
